  "guide.menu.title": "Guide",
  "guide.menu.heading": "Player Guide",
  "guide.menu.subtitle": "Learn the game faster, understand what each system is doing, and find answers without hunting through random screens.",
  "guide.menu.quickStart.title": "Quick Start Tour",
  "guide.menu.quickStart.subtitle": "A short guided intro to the game loop, core stats, businesses, and studio play.",
  "guide.menu.handbook.title": "Handbook",
  "guide.menu.handbook.subtitle": "Where things are, what they do, why they matter, and how to think about them.",
  "guide.menu.playbooks.title": "Playbooks",
  "guide.menu.playbooks.subtitle": "How to think through career, studio, money, and connected-story decisions without spoiling exact outcomes.",
  "guide.menu.faq.title": "FAQ",
  "guide.menu.faq.subtitle": "Quick answers to the questions players ask most often.",
  "guide.wizard.step": "Step {current} / {total}",
  "guide.wizard.next": "Next",
  "guide.wizard.finish": "Finish Tour",
  "guide.wizard.welcome.title": "Welcome to Actor Empire",
  "guide.wizard.welcome.body": "You are building a life, not just chasing one role. The best saves balance career, money, fame, relationships, studio power, and long-term planning.",
  "guide.wizard.weeklyLoop.title": "Your Weekly Loop",
  "guide.wizard.weeklyLoop.body": "Each week is a resource puzzle. Spend energy on acting, social growth, business, or personal life, then age up to see the results.",
  "guide.wizard.career.title": "Build the Career First",
  "guide.wizard.career.body": "CastLink, rehearsals, better agents, and strong performances open the entertainment ladder. Early on, steady work and smart role choices matter more than chasing only giant projects.",
  "guide.wizard.stats.title": "Know What Each Stat Does",
  "guide.wizard.stats.body": "Fame raises your profile. Reputation improves trust. Followers improve reach. Money gives you options. None of them fully replaces the others.",
  "guide.wizard.business.title": "Businesses Need Management",
  "guide.wizard.business.body": "Businesses do not print money by themselves. Pricing, hype, staffing, stock, and expansion all matter.",
  "guide.wizard.studio.title": "Production House is a Long Game",
  "guide.wizard.studio.body": "Your studio shines when you develop strong projects, manage releases, and turn wins into a library. Big payoffs can take time.",
  "guide.wizard.stories.title": "Connected Stories Need Care",
  "guide.wizard.stories.body": "Franchises and universes are powerful because characters, cast, sequels, crossovers, and market memory carry forward.",
  "guide.handbook.title": "Handbook",
  "guide.handbook.subtitle": "A plain-language reference for how the game works, what each system is for, and when to care about it.",
  "guide.handbook.gettingStarted.title": "Getting Started",
  "guide.handbook.gettingStarted.p1": "Your first goal is reliable momentum. Small wins in auditions, social activity, and money management usually beat risky all-in plays at the start.",
  "guide.handbook.gettingStarted.p2": "Think week to week. Every decision competes for time and energy, and spreading too thin slows progress everywhere.",
  "guide.handbook.gettingStarted.p3": "Use the phone apps often. CastLink grows your career, Team handles contracts, social apps build reach, and Guide explains the rest.",
  "guide.handbook.stats.title": "Stats Explained",
  "guide.handbook.stats.p1": "Fame is your public profile. It helps you get seen, land bigger opportunities, and stay culturally relevant.",
  "guide.handbook.stats.p2": "Reputation is how seriously the industry takes you. High reputation supports trust and better long-term outcomes.",
  "guide.handbook.stats.p3": "Followers are your social reach. They help influence, sponsorships, and online growth, but they cannot carry an acting career alone.",
  "guide.handbook.stats.p4": "Mood and energy shape how much you can do. A rich account means less if your character is exhausted or unhappy.",
  "guide.handbook.career.title": "Career Flow",
  "guide.handbook.career.p1": "CastLink is the main place to find work. Better talent, preparation, experience, and representation improve the quality of roles you can compete for.",
  "guide.handbook.career.p2": "Preparation matters. Rehearsals and smart role selection make performances more consistent.",
  "guide.handbook.career.p3": "Early game builds a record, mid game builds momentum, and late game is about leverage, choice, and legacy.",
  "guide.handbook.weeklyLoop.title": "Weekly Loop & Energy",
  "guide.handbook.weeklyLoop.p1": "Energy is weekly fuel. Acting, social moves, business work, and personal actions all draw from it.",
  "guide.handbook.weeklyLoop.p2": "Do not waste empty weeks. If you are waiting on a project, build fame, relationships, skills, or business progress.",
  "guide.handbook.weeklyLoop.p3": "Recovery has value. Sometimes restoring your character makes the next few weeks stronger.",
  "guide.handbook.social.title": "Fame, Followers & Social",
  "guide.handbook.social.p1": "Social media keeps you visible and can support your broader entertainment career.",
  "guide.handbook.social.p2": "Different platforms do different jobs: image, reach, conversation, and monetization.",
  "guide.handbook.social.p3": "Use social with purpose. Not every post needs to chase virality.",
  "guide.handbook.relationships.title": "Relationships & Networking",
  "guide.handbook.relationships.p1": "Professional relationships can change the quality of opportunities you see.",
  "guide.handbook.relationships.p2": "Personal relationships are not just flavor. Neglect can create drama, while healthy bonds support a stronger life path.",
  "guide.handbook.relationships.p3": "Networking works best over time. Repeated effort usually beats one expensive gesture.",
  "guide.handbook.businesses.title": "Businesses",
  "guide.handbook.businesses.p1": "Businesses are long-term income engines. Some are steady service businesses, while product businesses reward hands-on management.",
  "guide.handbook.businesses.p2": "Pricing, quality, hype, staffing, stock, and expansion all matter.",
  "guide.handbook.businesses.p3": "Marketing works best when product, capacity, and setup are already healthy.",
  "guide.handbook.productionHouse.title": "Production House",
  "guide.handbook.productionHouse.p1": "Think in stages: development, production, release, and afterlife all matter.",
  "guide.handbook.productionHouse.p2": "Not every project should be rushed. Stronger planning can beat forcing everything out quickly.",
  "guide.handbook.productionHouse.p3": "Your library matters. Over time, the studio becomes more valuable when you build a catalog instead of relying on one hit.",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.title": "Development Lab",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.p1": "Vault stores saved scripts and concepts until you are ready to develop, sell, or produce them.",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.p2": "Concept is where you shape genre, tone, audience, and story identity.",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.p3": "Market is where scripts can be bought or discovered. Watch format, genre, quality, and any known subject or franchise hook.",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.noteTitle": "No exact formula",
  "guide.handbook.developmentLab.noteBody": "The guide explains what matters, not the hidden math. Strong concepts usually come from fit, clarity, and timing.",
