  "services.role.review.author": "Critic {index}",
  "services.role.review.publication": "The Daily Review",
  "services.role.review.subjectPhrase.biopic": " of {subjectName}",
  "services.role.review.subjectStory.named": "{subjectName}'s story",
  "services.role.review.subjectStory.default": "The subject",
  "services.role.review.positive.general": "A stunning entry in the {genre} genre. {playerName} shines. || Confident, polished, and powered by a strong central performance from {playerName}. || The craft holds up, and the best moments feel genuinely cinematic. || A crowd-pleaser with enough heart to survive beyond opening weekend.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.general": "Has its moments, but fails to stick the landing. || Strong pieces are here, but the movie never fully becomes the event it wants to be. || The ambition is visible, even when the execution wobbles. || There is a good movie inside this, but it needed sharper structure.",
  "services.role.review.negative.general": "A disappointing mess. Avoid. || Too loud, too thin, and not nearly as memorable as the budget suggests. || The spectacle is expensive, but the drama feels undercooked. || A glossy package with very little staying power.",
  "services.role.review.thinCast": "For a movie this big, the world feels strangely empty around the leads. || The lead pair works, but the missing ensemble makes the scale feel smaller than the budget. || A stronger supporting cast could have made this feel like a real event.",
  "services.role.review.positive.MUSICAL": "The songs actually carry story, and {playerName} gives the musical its pulse. || The choreography, vocals, and emotional arc finally move as one.",
  "services.role.review.positive.BIOPIC": "{playerName} finds the person beneath the public myth{subjectPhrase}. || A thoughtful biopic anchored by transformation rather than imitation.",
  "services.role.review.positive.SPORTS": "The sports scenes have impact because the emotional stakes are clear. || A sincere underdog story that lets {playerName} play grit without losing vulnerability.",
  "services.role.review.positive.DOCUMENTARY": "{subjectStory} is handled with access, tension, and real curiosity. || The documentary earns its urgency by asking hard questions instead of selling easy answers.",
  "services.role.review.positive.MYSTERY": "The mystery pays off because the clues feel planted, not cheated. || A tightly wound mystery that lets {playerName} play suspicion, restraint, and discovery.",
  "services.role.review.positive.ANIMATION": "The animation has personality, not just polish. || A visually warm animated film with a performance from {playerName} that still registers through the craft.",
  "services.role.review.positive.CRIME": "The crime plotting is tight, morally uneasy, and built with real momentum. || A sharp crime story that understands consequence as much as suspense.",
  "services.role.review.positive.FANTASY": "The fantasy world feels lived in, and the lore supports the emotion instead of burying it. || A richly built fantasy that gives the spectacle a human center.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.MUSICAL": "The numbers are catchy, but the book scenes between them are uneven.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.BIOPIC": "The performance is committed, though the biopic keeps smoothing out the messier truths.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.SPORTS": "The sports drama is sincere, but too many beats feel familiar.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.DOCUMENTARY": "The access is valuable, but the argument could be sharper.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.MYSTERY": "The clues are intriguing, but the final reveal lands softer than the setup.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.ANIMATION": "The visual identity is strong, even when the story feels thin.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.CRIME": "The crime mechanics work, but the characters needed more interior life.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.FANTASY": "The world is imaginative, but the lore sometimes crowds out the drama.",
  "services.role.review.negative.MUSICAL": "The songs stop the movie cold instead of lifting it.",
  "services.role.review.negative.BIOPIC": "A surface-level biopic that mistakes makeup for insight.",
  "services.role.review.negative.SPORTS": "The sports scenes lack authenticity, and the drama never finds a second gear.",
  "services.role.review.negative.DOCUMENTARY": "The documentary has a subject, but not a point of view.",
  "services.role.review.negative.MYSTERY": "A mystery with suspects, but no real sense of discovery.",
  "services.role.review.negative.ANIMATION": "The animation is busy, but the emotional design is missing.",
  "services.role.review.negative.CRIME": "A crime story with twists but no tension.",
  "services.role.review.negative.FANTASY": "The fantasy world is expensive, confusing, and strangely weightless.",
  "services.role.review.positive.ANIME": "The anime style brings kinetic emotion and a distinct visual rhythm. || A strong anime feature that understands fandom without pandering to it.",
  "services.role.review.mixed.ANIME": "The anime craft is exciting, though the pacing occasionally overwhelms the character work.",
  "services.role.review.negative.ANIME": "The anime influence is visible, but the film never earns its intensity.",
  "services.role.review.recast.positive": "The new cast breathes fresh life into the franchise. A stunning entry in the {genre} genre.",
  "services.role.review.recast.mixed": "The recasting is jarring, but it has its moments.",
  "services.role.review.recast.negative": "A disastrous recast ruins whatever magic the original had. Avoid.",
